The conjecture is true! Here is a proof.

Axiom 1 (ax3): rdiv(op(X, Y), Y) = X.
Axiom 2 (ax2): ldiv(X, op(X, Y)) = Y.
Axiom 3 (ax1): op(X, ldiv(X, Y)) = Y.
Axiom 4 (ax5): op(op(X, Y), op(Z, Z)) = op(op(X, op(Y, Z)), Z).

Lemma 5: rdiv(op(op(X, Y), op(Z, Z)), Z) = op(X, op(Y, Z)).
Proof:
  rdiv(op(op(X, Y), op(Z, Z)), Z)
= { by axiom 4 (ax5) }
  rdiv(op(op(X, op(Y, Z)), Z), Z) (peak)
= { by axiom 1 (ax3) }
  op(X, op(Y, Z))

Lemma 6: op(op(X, Y), op(ldiv(Y, Z), ldiv(Y, Z))) = op(op(X, Z), ldiv(Y, Z)).
Proof:
  op(op(X, Y), op(ldiv(Y, Z), ldiv(Y, Z)))
= { by axiom 4 (ax5) }
  op(op(X, op(Y, ldiv(Y, Z))), ldiv(Y, Z)) (peak)
= { by axiom 3 (ax1) }
  op(op(X, Z), ldiv(Y, Z))

Lemma 7: op(ldiv(X, X), ldiv(X, X)) = ldiv(X, X).
Proof:
  op(ldiv(X, X), ldiv(X, X))
= { by axiom 2 (ax2) R->L }
  ldiv(op(Y, X), op(op(Y, X), op(ldiv(X, X), ldiv(X, X)))) (peak)
= { by lemma 6 }
  ldiv(op(Y, X), op(op(Y, X), ldiv(X, X)))
= { by axiom 2 (ax2) }
  ldiv(X, X)

Lemma 8: op(X, op(Y, ldiv(Z, Z))) = op(X, Y).
Proof:
  op(X, op(Y, ldiv(Z, Z)))
= { by lemma 5 R->L }
  rdiv(op(op(X, Y), op(ldiv(Z, Z), ldiv(Z, Z))), ldiv(Z, Z)) (peak)
= { by lemma 7 }
  rdiv(op(op(X, Y), ldiv(Z, Z)), ldiv(Z, Z))
= { by axiom 1 (ax3) }
  op(X, Y)

Lemma 9: op(X, ldiv(Y, Y)) = X.
Proof:
  op(X, ldiv(Y, Y))
= { by axiom 2 (ax2) R->L }
  ldiv(Z, op(Z, op(X, ldiv(Y, Y)))) (peak)
= { by lemma 8 }
  ldiv(Z, op(Z, X))
= { by axiom 2 (ax2) }
  X

Lemma 10: ldiv(Y, Y) = ldiv(X, X).
Proof:
  ldiv(Y, Y)
= { by axiom 2 (ax2) R->L }
  ldiv(X, op(X, ldiv(Y, Y))) (peak)
= { by lemma 9 }
  ldiv(X, X)

Goal 1 (goal): ldiv(sk_a, sk_a) = ldiv(sk_b, sk_b).
Proof:
  ldiv(sk_a, sk_a)
= { by lemma 10 }
  ldiv(sk_b, sk_b) (peak)

RESULT: Unsatisfiable (the axioms are contradictory).
